      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Consume Flesh",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "manipulate"
      ],
      "text": "Requirements The Canker cultist is adjacent to the corpse of a creature that died within the last hour, or is carrying a specially prepared lump of decaying flesh.\n\n---\n\nEffect The Canker cultist devours a chunk of the corpse or the lump of decaying flesh and regains Hit Points. They regain 1d6 healing Hit Points from consuming the flesh of a creature that died within the last hour, and 2d6 healing Hit Points from the lump.\n\nThe cultist can regain Hit Points from any given corpse only once."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Ghoul Fever",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "disease"
      ],
      "text": "Saving Throw DC 20 Fortitude save\n\n---\n\nStage 1 carrier with no ill effect (1 day)\n\nStage 2 2d6 void damage and regains half as many Hit Points from all healing (1 day)\n\nStage 3 as stage 2 (1 day)\n\nStage 4 2d6 void damage and gains no benefit from healing (1 day)\n\nStage 5 as stage 4 (1 day)\n\nStage 6 dead, and rises as a Ghoul the next midnight."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Paralysis",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "incapacitation",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Any living, non-elf creature hit by a Canker cultist's attack must succeed at a DC 20 Fortitude save save or become Paralyzed. It can attempt a new save at the end of each of its turns, and the DC cumulatively decreases by 1 on each such save."
    },
